{{Quote|Set for stun. I want them all alive. We'll need an ion blaster.|[[Alecia Beck]]|<ref name="Smuggler's Run">''[[Smuggler's Run: A Han Solo & Chewbacca Adventure]]''</ref>}}
'''Ion blasters''',<ref name="DB" /> also known as '''ionization blasters''',<ref name="USW" /> and '''Droid blaster''',<ref name="BB Episode Guide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-bad-batch-episode-guide|text="The Bad Batch" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref> were handheld weapons used by the [[Jawa]]s of [[Tatooine]] while hunting for salvage. These customized [[blaster]]s fired particles of ionized energy to disable the electrical systems of droids, rendering them powerless. When used against living creatures, they could be used as [[stun]] weapons.

==Description==
The ion [[blaster]]s carried by [[Jawa]] [[scavenger]]s of [[Tatooine]] were handcrafted,<ref name="USW" /> customized models built from salvaged parts,<ref name="DB" /> including parts from the [[CA-87 blaster]],<ref name="Blasters and Firearms" /> a retrofitted [[Jawa ionization blaster]]<ref name="Battlefront">''[[Star Wars Battlefront]]''</ref> and the [[PK-32 droid blaster]] was a model of droid blaster.<ref name="BB Episode Guide" /> The [[species]] typically began with a stripped-down blaster [[Power cell|power pack]], and added components such as an [[accu-accelerator]], scrounged from a [[starship]]'s [[ion engine]], and a [[restraining bolt]] from a [[droid]]. These pieces were added to the weapon's firing mechanism, giving the [[blaster pistol]] an accurate range of up to twelve [[meter]]s. The blasters were fitted with a safety button located above the trigger,<ref name="USW" /> and discharged blasts of ionized particles that disrupted the electronic systems of droids, causing the units to shut down.<ref name="DB" /> They could also be employed to stun living beings, in order to keep enemies alive.<ref name="Smuggler's Run" />

==History==
{{Quote|We're doomed!|[[C-3PO]]'s response to seeing an ion blaster|<ref name="ANH">{{Film|IV}}</ref>}}
Ion weapons were a long-established technology in [[the galaxy]], ranging from larger ranged weapons such as the [[T-7 ion disruptor rifle]] to massive [[planet]]-based [[ion cannon]]s. The [[Jawa]] ion [[blaster]]s were created using the same principle, and were carried by the [[scavenger]]s during salvage runs on the [[desert]] planet of [[Tatooine]].<ref name="DB" /> The [[astromech droid]] [[R2-D2]] was hit by an ion blaster after being discovered in the [[Jundland Wastes]] by a group of Jawas, who carried the droid back to their [[sandcrawler]].<ref name="ANH" /> A Jawa brought an ion blaster to bear on [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] when the [[Sith Lord]] visited [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]] in [[Boba Fett's Palace|his palace]] on Tatooine, but was killed when Vader deflected the weapon's green bolt back into its owner.<ref name="Vader 1">[[Darth Vader (2015) 1|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 1]]</ref> 

A group of Jawas used their ion blasters to defend themselves against the [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] after he attempted to board their sandcrawler. While Djarin would succeed in climbing on top of the sandcrawler, he was almost instantly stunned by a series of ion blasters firing simultaneously, causing him to fall onto the ground below.<ref name="Chapter 2">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 2: The Child}}</ref>

